# CELL: `.map()` × bare-param recv × Option[String] → Option[int]
# GRADUATED Round XV Track B — retired `has_string_coercion` bail so XIV
# adapter owns String payloads (methods.rs try_lower_option_result_combinator).
# PRE-FIX (RED-verified at HEAD e7abec29 / known_gap path, C and LLVM):
#   C: exit=1, stdout blank-line then `hi`, stderr
#     `gorget_string_free invariant: cap=… but alloc=NULL`
#   LLVM: exit 139, empty stdout
# PRE-FIX MECHANISM (refined, scout /tmp/xv_scoutB_string_coercion.md):
#   Bail returned None from the adapter → C-inline fallback. GIR typed result
#   local `r` as Option[GorgetString] (receiver type) not Option[int] →
#   size-mismatched memcpy + String free on garbage. Mapped `2` never printed;
#   receiver readback often still printed `hi`. L2020 `!is_last_use` clone is a
#   non-firing sibling on bare-param (Ptr type fails is_resource_type).
# INTENDED: `2\nhi`, exit 0.
# AXIS SAMPLE: payload=String · combinator=map · ret=int · recv=bare-param.
# OMIT-LIST (same bail site; capacity): filter / unwrap_or_else / or_else
# String; Result[String,String].map (possible accidental size-overlap — not
# coverage). See siblings for other cells.
# FORMER NAME: known_gaps/sound_option_string_coercion_map_param.gg

void call_it(Option[String] p):
    Option[int] r = p.map((String s): s.len())
    if r is Some(v):
        print(v)
    if p is Some(s2):
        print(s2)

void main():
    call_it(Some("hi"))
